 activation of neonatal CD11c&#x0002b; dendritic cells and induction of adult-like CD8&#x0002b; cytotoxic T cell responses by synthetic microspheres.</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><volume>173</volume><fpage>2669</fpage><lpage>2674</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15294984</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003683-Schellack1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schellack</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Prinz</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Egyed</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Fritz</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Wittmann</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>IC31, a novel adjuvant signaling via TLR9, induces potent cellular and humoral immune responses.</article-title><source>Vaccine</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>5461</fpage><lpage>5472</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16678312</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003683-Riedl1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Riedl</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Riedl</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>von Gabain</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Nagy</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Lingnau</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>The novel adjuvant IC31 strongly improves influenza vaccine-specific cellular and humoral immune responses in young adult and aged mice.</article-title><source>Vaccine</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>3461</fpage><lpage>3468</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18495302</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003683-WeinrichOlsen1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"